# Copilot Ignore Configuration
# This file controls what files GitHub Copilot can access for context in VSCode
# Syntax similar to .gitignore, but with negative patterns to explicitly include files

# By default, Copilot respects .gitignore, but we can override it here
# to make Unreal Engine logs accessible for debugging and assistance

# Include ALL log files for Copilot context (even though they're in .gitignore)
# This allows Copilot to see UE output logs for better debugging assistance
!*.log
!**/*.log

# Specifically include common UE log locations
!Saved/Logs/*.log
!*/Saved/Logs/*.log

# Include test logs for debugging test failures
!tests/*.log
!tests/**/*.log

# However, exclude very large or binary log files that might overwhelm Copilot
# Copilot works best with files under 1MB. Exclude larger logs or crash dumps.
# (You can adjust this based on your project needs)
*.dmp
*.crash

# Exclude build logs that are too verbose
**/Intermediate/Build/**/*.log

# Keep sensitive logs private (add patterns as needed)
# Example: !**/Credentials/*.log
